  "summary": "A San Mateo County Civil Grand Jury report found no current out-of-state ALPR data sharing by county police agencies as of December 2025, but identified insufficient audit and oversight mechanisms and documented data sharing with private university security by agencies including Atherton, Belmont, Brisbane, Burlingame, Colma, East Palo Alto, Hillsborough, Menlo Park, Pacifica, Redwood City, San Bruno, and the Sheriff's Office. San Mateo PD and the Sheriff's Office responded describing audit and safeguard processes.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Although the materials reviewed did not identify current sharing by SMC operators with out-of-state entities, most operators did not document criteria, process, or controls governing in-state sharing in a manner sufficient to demonstrate compliance with law",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "As the size of a network increases and more law enforcement agencies are granted access, the risk of misuse correspondingly increases",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    },
    {
      "quote": "The ALPR system is configured by the Sheriff's Office with safeguards that prevent access by out-of-state and federal agencies. Compliance is verified through periodic audits conducted by Sheriff's Office personnel",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
